  "number": "5.4.8",
  "title": "Check Your Understanding",
  "body": " Check Your Understanding    Which statement about C++ structures and classes is true?      Only classes can contain member functions.    Both structures and classes can contain member functions.      Both structures and classes can contain data members and member functions.    In C++, both can represent objects with state and behavior.      Structures can contain data, while classes can contain only functions.    Both structures and classes can contain data and functions.        What is the default access for members of a struct ?     public   Members of a structure are public by default.     private   Members of a class are private by default.     const    const describes whether something may be modified; it is not an access level.        What is the default access for members of a class ?     public   Public is the default for a structure, not a class.     private   Members of a class are private by default.     protected    protected is another access level, but it is not the default for a class.        Why might a programmer choose a class instead of exposing all data members publicly?      Because structures cannot contain functions.    Structures can contain member functions in C++.      To control how outside code accesses and changes the object's state.    Controlling access to internal state is an important reason for using classes.      Because class objects do not contain data members.    Classes can contain data members just like structures.        Which type is the stronger candidate for a class according to the design guideline in this section?      A Point that simply stores public x and y coordinates.    A small type whose purpose is primarily to group related data is often a reasonable use of a struct .      A Thermostat that should control how its temperature setting is changed.    A class is a natural choice when the type should provide operations that control access to its internal state.      Any type that contains at least one member function.    Structures can contain member functions too, so the presence of a member function alone does not require a class.        What does it mean to say that a class provides an abstraction ?      Every detail of the object's representation must be visible to code that uses it.    Abstraction allows users of a type to work through its interface without depending on every implementation detail.      Outside code can focus on what the object can do without needing to know every detail of how its state is stored.    The public operations describe how to use the object while implementation details can remain hidden.      All objects of the class share one copy of their data.    Each object has its own state. Abstraction concerns the boundary between how an object is used and how it is implemented.      "
