  "number": "5.11.5",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Which statement about a member function is true?     It is declared as part of a structure or class and can be called on an object of that type.  Correct. The object appears before the dot when the function is called.    It must always receive the current object as an explicit parameter.  The current object is an implicit part of a member-function call.    It can only read data members and cannot modify them.  Non-const member functions can modify the current object's data members.    It cannot be defined outside the class or structure definition.  A member function can be defined outside using the scope resolution operator.    "
